infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Naive backfill vs batched backfill
  desc Same UPDATE on 100M rows — two very different blast radii
  compares
    - label Naive
      children
        - label 40 GB WAL in 10 min
          desc 1 WAL record per row, no breathing room
        - label Replica lag 120s+
          desc replicas cannot replay WAL fast enough
        - label Stale standby reads
          desc endpoints return contradicting rows
        - label Query cancellations
          desc lag past max_standby_streaming_delay
    - label Batched
      children
        - label Bounded WAL per txn
          desc 1k-10k rows per batch + pg_sleep(0.1)
        - label Replica lag near zero
          desc replicas keep up between batches
        - label Consistent reads
          desc standby stays caught up
        - label Slow when lag over 10s
          desc monitor replay_lag, throttle batches
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
